li.t:
the candidate was not a duplicate caught at check 2 (an exact retained
statement: the first copy was already answered, and a replay on the path must
not draw a second notice);

a reserved record is decided then, under the configuration in
force at recovery (the receiver has no older one it can trust), and then takes
effect;

MUST produce Peer Notices valid against the peer-notice schema
(), and MUST confirm that its own emitted Peer Notices
satisfy the same schema the valid peer-* fixtures satisfy;

MUST refuse to emit into peer/ any document that would fail that
schema, and MUST NOT emit a peer document into inbound/
();

